{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following MS C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original MS C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\nusing ld = long double;\n\nll my_gcd(ll a, ll b) {\n    for (ll t; b; t = b, b = a % b, a = t);\n    return a;\n}\n\nll my_lcm(ll a, ll b) {\n    return a / my_gcd(a, b) * b;\n}\n\nld my_diff(ll n1, ll d1, ll n2, ll d2) {\n    ll cd = my_lcm(d1, d2);\n    ll num1 = cd / d1 * n1;\n    ll num2 = cd / d2 * n2;\n    return abs(num1 - num2) / ld(cd);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n#ifndef ONLINE_JUDGE\n    freopen(\"input.txt\", \"r\", stdin);\n    freopen(\"output.txt\", \"w\", stdout);\n#endif\n\n    ll x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    ll best_n = 0, best_d = 1;\n    ld target = ld(x) / y;\n    \n    for (ll d = 1; d <= n; ++d) {\n        ll left = 1, right = 1000000;\n        while (right - left > 1) {\n            ll mid = (left + right) / 2;\n            ld val = ld(mid) / d;\n            if (val < target) left = mid;\n            else right = mid;\n        }\n        \n        ll candidate = (my_diff(left, d, x, y) > my_diff(right, d, x, y)) ? right : left;\n        if (my_diff(candidate, d, x, y) < my_diff(best_n, best_d, x, y)) {\n            best_n = candidate;\n            best_d = d;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << best_n << \"/\" << best_d;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        \n        long x = scanner.nextLong();\n        long y = scanner.nextLong();\n        long n = scanner.nextLong();\n        \n        long best_n = 0;\n        long best_d = 1;\n        double target = (double) x / y;\n        \n        for (long d = 1; d <= n; ++d) {\n            long left = 1;\n            long right = 1000000;\n            while (right - left > 1) {\n                long mid = (left + right) / 2;\n                double val = (double) mid / d;\n                if (val < target) {\n                    left = mid;\n                } else {\n                    right = mid;\n                }\n            }\n            \n            long candidate = (myDiff(left, d, x, y) > myDiff(right, d, x, y)) ? right : left;\n            if (myDiff(candidate, d, x, y) < myDiff(best_n, best_d, x, y)) {\n                best_n = candidate;\n                best_d = d;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(best_n + \"/\" + best_d);\n    }\n    \n    public static long myGcd(long a, long b) {\n        while (b != 0) {\n            long t = b;\n            b = a % b;\n            a = t;\n        }\n        return a;\n    }\n    \n    public static long myLcm(long a, long b) {\n        return a / myGcd(a, b) * b;\n    }\n    \n    public static double myDiff(long n1, long d1, long n2, long d2) {\n        long cd = myLcm(d1, d2);\n        long num1 = cd / d1 * n1;\n        long num2 = cd / d2 * n2;\n        return Math.abs(num1 - n